  "summary": "Priorities, cross-fades, loops and stopping. idle loops (1 s, fades 0.5 s) and fires events at 0 and 0.5 s of every loop, including all loops passed in one long frame (dt = 2.5). wave (normal, 1.5 s, fades 0.5 s) replaces it: idle fades out while wave fades in, blending with lerp over idle's result; Arm has its own fade_in of 0 and jumps to 1. A request with a lower priority (idle) is refused while wave plays and accepted once wave has finished; a force request replaces a normal motion; stop_motions fades out every motion. When a motion ends, its last applied values stay (they are part of the base values).",
